    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d944">

                <pb facs="0874" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 C and M Alliance/78: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-01T08:00:00+08:00">March 1, 1940—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 1—6:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Reference my 10, February 4, 5 p.m., and 18, February 23, 6 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="51" xml:id="d944-f1"/> burning of property at Lungchow. The French Consul
                    at <pb facs="0875" n="867" xml:id="pg867"/> Lungchow has now informed French
                    Consul here that the Chinese forces had evacuated Lungchow and environs more
                    than 48 hours before the burning of the Christian and Missionary Alliance
                    property on December 23, 1939.</p>
                <p>Continuing representations are being made to Japanese Consul General.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
